    NASA material is generally not subject to copyright in the United States.
    Credit NASA and do not imply NASA endorsement (NASA Images and Media
    Usage Guidelines: https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/).
  - Moon globe (models/planets/moon_small.glb): supplied by Team RealPugs.
    Its original source and licence must be confirmed by the team before publication.
  - The files in models/optimized/ are compressed copies of the originals
    (gltf-transform 4.5.1: meshopt geometry, WebP textures). The originals are unchanged.

Images (images/)
  - images/moon and images/mars: resized copies of the pictures shown on the
    azmth.space mission pages. Each keeps the credit and the link to its original,
    recorded in data/image-index.json and shown next to the picture on the site.
    The CC BY 4.0 licence of the catalogue does NOT cover these photographs; every
    entry is flagged VERIFY_BEFORE_PUBLICATION until its original licence is checked.
  - images/team: the RealPugs emblem and the team photo, supplied by Team RealPugs.

Data
  - Moon and Mars mission catalogues: azmth.space, licensed CC BY 4.0
    ("according to azmth.space's catalogue of Moon landing and impact sites";
    Mars catalogue at https://azmth.space/mars/missions). Data as of 2 November 2026; pages fetched on 14 November 2026
    (see data/build-report.json). Page records in data/missions keep the catalogue's
    wording for facts, timelines and source lists.
  - Scientific papers, NASA reports and agency documents are linked, not reproduced.
    Every source is listed on the site's References page with its title, author,
    year, document type and a direct link.
